#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:0
msgid ""
"Understand snap performance, including timing install and refresh "
"operations, analysing SquashFS performance, and comparing compression "
"algorithms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:8
msgid "Snap performance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:10
msgid ""
"The performance of a running application should not be affected by its snap "
"environment, and any  performance or system monitoring tool will work on "
"snapped processes in exactly the same way they would on other applications "
"and processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:12
msgid ""
"But monitoring specific snap operations, alongside installation and "
"distribution performance, can help with both snap _packaging_ and "
"_configuration_ decisions, and also help to discover potential performance "
"issues outside of an application's control. Several such approaches are "
"outlined below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:14
msgid ""
"On devices running Ubuntu Core, a [kernel boot parameter](https://"
"documentation.ubuntu.com/core/reference/kernel-boot-parameters/#ubuntu-core-"
"bootchart) can be used to generate a bootchart showing system startup times "
"and performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:16
msgid "Snap debug timing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:18
msgid ""
"Timing output from a snap can be a useful measure of overall performance, "
"but it can also reveal performance bottlenecks and targets for improvement. "
"The {ref}`snap debug <how-to-guides-fix-common-issues-debug-snaps>` command "
"includes several options to produce timing output for execution time, "
"internal _ensure_ activities and subsystem startup times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:20
msgid "Execution time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:22
msgid ""
"By default, the `snap debug timings` command will produce timing output for "
"a specific _change_, which itself represents a set of operations performed "
"by the snap daemon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:24
msgid "The syntax for the command is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:26
msgid "snap debug timings <change-id>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:30
msgid ""
"The change identifiers (`<change-id>`) are listed under the `ID` column in "
"the output to `snap changes`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:32
msgid ""
"ID    Status  Spawn                   Ready                   Summary\n"
"8302  Done    yesterday at 18:24 BST  yesterday at 18:24 BST  Install "
"\"chromium\" snap\n"
"8303  Done    today at 11:46 BST      today at 11:46 BST      Remove hotplug "
"connections and slots of device /dev/ttyACM0 (100 Series/C230 …; serial: "
"6564B3891339) with interface \"serial-port\"\n"
"8304  Done    today at 11:50 BST      today at 11:50 BST      Add hotplug "
"slot of interface \"/dev/ttyACM0 (100 Series/C230 …; serial: 6564B3891339)\" "
"for device serial-port with hotplug key \"056a4e841487…\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:39
msgid ""
"Instead of a change id,  the `--last` argument can be used with a well "
"defined name for a change, such as `auto-refresh`, `install`, `refresh`, "
"`remove` or `try`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:41
msgid ""
"With the `--verbose` argument, the output will also include a label for the "
"change:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:43
msgid ""
"ID     Status Doing  Undoing  Label          Summary\n"
"160162 Done   750ms        -  prerequisites  Ensure prerequisites for "
"\"chromium\" are available\n"
"^             681ms        -  install-prereq install \"cups\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-performance.md:49
msgid ""
"The ID represents a numerical identifier for tasks spawned by the change "
"logic, with nested tasks denoted with the `^` symbol beneath their parent."
msgstr ""

